  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  headerText: {fileID: 1063043626868478173}
  descriptionText: {fileID: 3151724391876236131}
  text1: Rocker Arm Assembly
  text2: The rocker arm is a critical component in the valve train of an internal
    combustion engine. It transfers motion from the camshaft (via pushrods) to the
    valves, enabling them to open and close. The orange line indicates the motion
    path between the camshaft and the valves.
